---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Roadmap — CloudOps Guard"
  description="An honest account of what CloudOps Guard has released, what is implemented in this website's build but not yet deployed, and what is still planned or absent."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="status-label status-label--neutral">Roadmap</p>
      <h1>Roadmap</h1>
      <p>
        This page distinguishes three different kinds of "done": what has actually been released as a
        command-line tool, what exists in this website's current build but has not been deployed, and
        what is still planned or entirely absent. No date, commitment, subscription, or SaaS
        availability is implied by anything below.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="released-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="released-heading">Released CLI capabilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Kubernetes audit (v0.1.0)</strong> &mdash; a read-only command-line audit of a
          cluster's namespaces, pods, deployments, and replica sets.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitLab CI/CD audit (v0.2.0)</strong> &mdash; a read-only, single-project command-line
          audit of branch protection, merge-request policy, CI/CD settings, and job/service image
          references.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Both are available today as the <code>cloudops-guard</code> command-line tool.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="implemented-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="implemented-heading">Implemented in this website's build, not yet deployed</h2>
      <p>
        The following exist in this website's current source and build output. <strong
          >None of it has been deployed, released, or published</strong
        > &mdash; it is reachable only by someone running the build themselves.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Interactive Kubernetes and GitLab demonstrations, using fixed synthetic data.</li>
        <li>Browser-side comparison between two scan states (new/persistent/resolved findings).</li>
        <li>A deterministic, non-AI-generated executive summary view.</li>
        <li>
          A local report explorer that opens a <code>report.json</code> file the CLI already produced,
          entirely in the browser, never uploaded.
        </li>
        <li>This searchable check catalogue and the product/educational pages around it.</li>
        <li>
          A <a href="/request-demo">pilot-request form</a> and a <a href="/feedback">feedback form</a>,
          each backed by an isolated server-side endpoint with mandatory bot-verification and email
          delivery &mdash; structurally isolated from report data (see <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>)
          and not yet connected to a real, deployed mail service.
        </li>
        <li>
          Automated accessibility scanning (axe, across every route) and a three-browser
          (Chromium/Firefox/WebKit) Playwright test matrix, run in CI on every change.
        </li>
        <li>
          Deployment <em>configuration</em> for this website (a Wrangler configuration renderer and a
          manually-dispatched, credential-gated GitHub Actions workflow) &mdash; this is configuration
          only; see the next section for what remains genuinely absent.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--muted" aria-labelledby="planned-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="planned-heading">Still planned or absent</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          An actual, authorized production deployment of this website &mdash; real Cloudflare
          account/domain/binding provisioning and dispatching the deployment workflow have not happened.
        </li>
        <li>AKS/EKS-specific integrations.</li>
        <li>Broader cloud cost analysis beyond the two GitLab cost-efficiency checks already implemented.</li>
        <li>A persistent, multi-tenant dashboard for viewing uploaded reports over time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>None of these exist yet in any form on this site.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="in-design-heading">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="in-design-heading">Specified, not implemented</h2>
      <p>
        A versioned report-ingestion API and an explicit, customer-controlled command-line uploader are
        specified in a published design document (v0.4.0, Phase 4A). <strong
          >This phase is documentation and contract design only</strong
        > &mdash; no API, storage, authentication, or uploader code exists, nothing is deployed, and this
        website does not and will not itself upload a report; the design is a separate service, entirely
        outside this site. See <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> for how this website's own no-upload
        behavior is unaffected.
      </p>
      <p>
        A later, uncommitted, pending-review Phase 4B has added local, in-memory reference storage and
        token-record code inside the CloudOps Guard Python package (not this website's codebase) &mdash;
        still no HTTP endpoint, no authentication, no uploader, no production storage, and nothing
        deployed anywhere. That work has no bearing on this site or its own no-upload behavior.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
